If I'm understanding the bug correctly, the only reason you never see an 
effect from this in normal play is that there's nothing in the vanilla 
game that depends on the lit/unlit status of the square on which you're 
standing when you're blind.  If The Dev Team were to add something that 
did this (as the Grue Challenge does in the Tournament, which is where 
Friedrich found this) then they would have to make this change as well. 
  Friedrich's suggestion is that it constitutes a bug because it leaves 
the game's idea of the world out of synch with where it should be and 
means that a future code change would have to make this fix or it would 
create player-visible buggy behavior.

Better to report it so it can at least be a reminder in the future, even 
if it's not deemed worthy of fixing now.

(I haven't tested his fix yet, but it seems likely that it wouldn't 
change any player-visible behavior in vanilla NetHack at all and would 
bring the game's idea of the world-state into line with where it should 
be.  I'll let you know how accurate that impression is when I can get 
some time to try it.)

